  "_design_r0": "Overlord Dropkick Startup: begins from open aerial combat guard, coils knees up while sweeping arms to snap cross over chest by frame 8, then explodes into horizontal dropkick at frame 15.",
  "_design": "Overlord dropkick startup (Fair, Big Band j.HK): f0 already breaks from the fall (knees up, arms lifting out), f1-f4 hard tuck (knees snap to the chest, arms thrown forward and wide, not twinned), f4-f11 the coil stays alive and rocks back, f12-f15 both legs shoot forward together (42% of the release on f14, 58% on f15 = first active frame), body lays back to near horizontal with a 28 deg barrel roll (left hip up) and 12 deg yaw so the legs read from behind, left arm flung overhead-back, right arm out-back-low, head curled up looking over the feet. f15 == loop f11.",
